# Kia Sportage fourth generation five-door, 2016-2022.
#
# The QL Sportage: the sharper, more sculpted body with the larger tiger-
# nose grille, the painted A-pillar and the conventional door handles. UK
# sales from February 2016; the 2018 facelift is a colour-run change.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kia_Sportage
#
# Dimensions 4.480 x 1.855 x 1.635-1.645 m, wheelbase 2.670 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true side elevation of a red five-door; the
# other images show a UK First Edition car in front and rear views.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK chart was found. Black, silver, white and red
# are plain names. Weights 18, 16, 14, 12, total 60, provisional.
#
# Speed 200 km/h. Comfort 90/465, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 90. Classes 1,2.
# Dates are road presence: 2016 intro, retires staggered 2034-2037.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/kia-sportage-4.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/kia-sportage-4.dae. References:
# citycars/references/kia-sportage-4/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: a thin bumper-corner tab is present but does not read at
# 128 px; the arch cladding is a heavy ring. The black roof is not modelled and
# the greenhouse is shallower than the photograph's. At 128 px the straight
# shoulder crease, wide tiger-nose and joined tail lamps read as a fourth-
# generation Sportage.


obj=citycar
name=KiaSportage4(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=18
intro_year=2016
intro_month=2
retire_year=2037
retire_month=6
speed=200
length=3
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=90
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=465

